- **D3: the proof of the chain policy is a cell that reads the handler's own TLS options through an internal property (Q3).** `TlsOptions => _handler.SslOptions` (the handler the client sends with, not a copy). `1-red.diff` adds that property WITH main's settings unchanged, so DA18's red is main's own configuration (`policy set False`). A behavioural cell cannot fail on main on this machine: the review's probe P07 measured 0 fetches on macOS without the policy (RELAYED from owed 79). DA18 also runs one pinned call to a leaf whose issuer the stub never sends, so the policy is proved not to break the pinned path. Alternative: reflection on private framework fields (fragile across .NET versions).
